@startuml LocalChat_Conceptual_Architecture
' General conceptual overview of LocalChat discovery and connection architecture.
' This diagram intentionally hides implementation details and focuses on DNS-SD/mDNS ideas.

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title LocalChat - conceptual architecture overview

node "Host A\nLocalChat node" as HostA {
  component "LocalChat App" as AppA
  component "Service Registration\nDNS-SD" as RegA
  component "Service Browsing\nDNS-SD" as BrowseA
  component "TCP Data Exchange\npeer-to-peer" as TcpA
  database "Local hostname\nHostA.local" as NameA

  AppA --> RegA : registers service
  AppA --> BrowseA : searches for peers
  AppA --> TcpA : starts sessions
  RegA ..> NameA : service target host
}

node "Host B\nLocalChat node" as HostB {
  component "LocalChat App" as AppB
  component "Service Registration\nDNS-SD" as RegB
  component "Service Browsing\nDNS-SD" as BrowseB
  component "TCP Data Exchange\npeer-to-peer" as TcpB
  database "Local hostname\nHostB.local" as NameB

  AppB --> RegB : registers service
  AppB --> BrowseB : searches for peers
  AppB --> TcpB : starts sessions
  RegB ..> NameB : service target host
}

cloud "Local network\nmulticast domain" as LAN {
  component "mDNS multicast\nUDP 5353" as MDNS
  component "DNS-SD records\nPTR / SRV / TXT" as DNSSD
  component "mDNS address records\nA / AAAA" as Addr
}

component "Local mDNS/DNS-SD daemon\nmDNSResponder / Avahi" as DaemonA
component "Local mDNS/DNS-SD daemon\nmDNSResponder / Avahi" as DaemonB

RegA --> DaemonA : register service instance
BrowseA --> DaemonA : browse / resolve peers
RegB --> DaemonB : register service instance
BrowseB --> DaemonB : browse / resolve peers

DaemonA <--> MDNS : multicast queries/responses
DaemonB <--> MDNS : multicast queries/responses
MDNS --> DNSSD : advertises service presence
MDNS --> Addr : resolves hostnames to IPs

TcpA <--> TcpB : direct TCP connection\nafter discovery and resolution

note bottom of LAN
DNS-SD describes available services on the LAN.
mDNS transports the queries/responses and resolves .local hostnames to IP addresses.
After discovery, LocalChat data is exchanged directly between hosts over TCP.
end note

@enduml

@startuml LocalChat_Discovery_And_Resolution_Flow
' Sequence-level view of the same idea.

skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox

title LocalChat - DNS-SD browsing and mDNS resolution flow

box "Host A" #LightBlue
participant "LocalChat App A" as AppA
participant "DNS-SD API A" as APIA
participant "mDNS/DNS-SD daemon A\nmDNSResponder / Avahi" as DaemonA
end box

participant "Local network\nmulticast mDNS\nUDP 5353" as LAN

box "Host B" #LightGreen
participant "mDNS/DNS-SD daemon B\nmDNSResponder / Avahi" as DaemonB
participant "DNS-SD API B" as APIB
participant "LocalChat App B" as AppB
end box

== Service registration ==
AppA -> APIA : Register service instance\n"HostA._localchat._tcp.local"\nport + optional TXT metadata
APIA -> DaemonA : Pass registration to local daemon
DaemonA -> LAN : Announce / answer for DNS-SD records\nPTR, SRV, TXT
note right of DaemonA
The service instance points to a target hostname,
for example HostA.local, and a TCP port.
end note

== Browsing discovers the service ==
AppB -> APIB : Browse for service type\n"_localchat._tcp.local"
APIB -> DaemonB : Start DNS-SD browse operation
DaemonB -> LAN : mDNS query:\nWho offers _localchat._tcp.local?
LAN --> DaemonB : Response:\nHostA._localchat._tcp.local exists
DaemonB --> APIB : Service discovered\ninstance + type + domain
APIB --> AppB : Notify application about Host A

== Resolving gets endpoint information ==
AppB -> APIB : Resolve discovered service instance
APIB -> DaemonB : Resolve via DNS-SD/mDNS
DaemonB -> LAN : Query SRV/TXT for service\nand A/AAAA for target hostname
LAN --> DaemonB : SRV: target hostname + port\nTXT: metadata\nA/AAAA: IP address
DaemonB --> APIB : Resolved endpoint
APIB --> AppB : IP address + port + metadata

== Direct data exchange ==
AppB -> AppA : Open direct TCP connection\nto resolved IP:port
AppA <--> AppB : Exchange LocalChat messages/files\nwithout a central server

note over AppA, AppB
The daemon participates only in discovery and name/address resolution.
The actual LocalChat communication is peer-to-peer over TCP.
end note

@enduml
